| 0083 | this port: the PHY and the pump set up as the factory driver sets them — the 800 µs hold of a frame's bit 0 is bit 6 of SC8547_REG_3A (0x3a), written 0x60 as the vendor does in every PHY setup, and 0x34 is left alone (the driver had the register transcribed wrong and worked by luck: 0x3a's power-on value has the bit set); the pump CONTROL writes carry bit 2 (0x84 / 0x04) as the vendor's do; the pump watchdog is armed at 1 s (REG_09 0x13) instead of 5 s; the adapter is called gone after 250 ms of silence while charging, 500 ms before the grant (the vendor's 200 ms; the brick's longest traced pause was 174 ms), 3000 ms before the first frame | John Stockdale | written 2026-11-04 (ledger rows 2–4, 8); checkpatch 0/0/0; **flown as flight D3 with the pump driver reloaded and the PHY trace on**: at setup `0x3a ← 0x60` and no write to 0x34 at all, at the enable `0x09 ← 0x13` and `0x07 ← 0x84`; no false "adapter gone" across 91 316 frames and no error flag on any frame (the decoder's only hit is the PHY's idle read before the first frame) — the hold on 0x3a leaves no error on a current command, as claimed; entered the series the same day |
