Numbering note: the number 0029 was first used on 2026-11-02 for infiniti's
ADSP reserved-memory change (0x4c00000 -> 0x5000000) and withdrawn the same
day — the OnePlus board file already deletes and redefines that node with
0x5000000, so it had no effect here (docs/porting-log.md, "0029 was a
no-op"). The number was then reused for the iris platform data.

Pin bump 2026-11-03 (rung P): 7c98a10e6bb7 → b7d639cfb282
-----------------------------------------------------------

The whole series was replayed with `git am -3` on Perpetua perpetua/v7.3 =
b7d639cfb282 (100 commits past the old pin) on 2026-11-02; 56 patches applied
untouched and four were re-diffed, replacing the same-numbered files here
(the interim copies lived in a p-pinbump/ directory until 2026-11-03, when
they were byte-identical to the series and the directory was removed):

- 0028: the READ_DONE half is upstream (9ba37ef1db70); the WRITE_DONE half
  is kept.
- 0031: the head moved the CPU thermal overrides into a shared include; the
  patch is now just the &iris block.
- 0058: the head added Xiaomi's pmic-glink match data next to ours; both kept. The re-diff kept the hBoost client keyed on "oplus,kaanapali-pmic-glink" although Perpetua 5ff346c547a7, before the pin, had renamed the board's compatible to "oneplus,kaanapali-pmic-glink" (generic fallback kept): on #45 the generic entry matched, no pmic_glink.hboost device was created and the pen charger read chip_id 0x0000 — found by the checkpoint audit on 2026-11-03 and corrected the same day (0058 now matches the renamed string; pmic_glink is built in, so the fix flies with build #46).
- 0061: the head added the SuperVOOC nodes (i2c_hub_0 charge pumps, PMK8850
  ADC channels, tlmm pump IRQ states) at the same insertion points as the
  pen charger's; both kept (i2c_hub_1, PMIC-GPIO states, gpio169 state).

0020 was retired at the same time: at the new pin Perpetua's TFA9865 driver
puts the two middle amplifiers in stock's playing state by itself (registers
5f:00e0 and 76:d700 read back on build #45), so the local patch had nothing
left to do. The number is not reused. The config fragments were re-merged
against the head's devices/iceland/kernel.config (ADC5 Gen3/Gen4,
CHARGER_SC8547, CHARGER_SC8547_SVOOC, oplus_svooc, and the lockup detectors
Denial added after two freezes during SuperVOOC). Build #45 (kernel 7.3.0+)
was RAM-booted and then flashed to boot_b on 2026-11-03.

Numbering: the ath12k regulatory series took 0064–0067 and the 11d-scan patch 0068 on 2026-11-03 (first flown as module swaps on #45/#46). The input-identity patch for the pen and touch devices was first
filed as 0043 on 2026-11-03, colliding with the first infiniti iris fix; it is
0063 since the same day (the series applies in lexical order, and it touches
only nt36xxx.c, which no later patch changes). It was written after build #45 had started: #45 applied 61 patch files and carries 0063's change in its nt36536 module, compiled by hand; the next build takes it from the series. The pogo keyboard series took 0087–0090 on 2026-11-04 (the Fedora port's 0094–0097, 0090 re-diffed), after the staged charging fixes 0079–0084 and the numbers 0085/0086 reserved for the PD PPS pair.
